\title{gllvmTMB: Fit Multivariate Models from Wide Response Data}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Fits multivariate models for data where each site, individual, species, or study has several responses. Start from a wide data frame with the 'traits()' formula interface, or from already-stacked long data, and estimate trait covariance, pairwise correlations, shared latent axes, and trait-specific variance. Binary presence-absence applications include binomial-family joint species distribution models. Optional animal, phylogenetic, spatial, and known-sampling-variance components use the same formula grammar. Model fitting uses Template Model Builder (Kristensen et al. 2016 \doi{10.18637/jss.v070.i05}). This experimental package should be used through its documented tutorials and model-specific boundaries; convergence alone does not establish that an estimate or interval is reliable.
}
